    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d291">

                <pb facs="0513" n="411" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg411"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.114 Newfoundland/121: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at St.
                        John’s</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Quarton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">St. John’s</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-02-13T13:00:00-03:30">February 13,
                            1935—1 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received February 13—12:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s telegram of February 12, 6 p.m.<anchor n="32" xml:id="d291-f1"/>
                    Commission of Government at a meeting yesterday afternoon February 12th approved
                    Bermuda system of landing certificates. It cannot become immediately effective
                    in Newfoundland without approval of the Dominions Office which has been
                    telegraphed for. Effective date will be telegraphed when known.<anchor n="33"
                        xml:id="d291-f2"/> It is understood this legislation is included with other
                    maritime and customs matters. Please regard foregoing as strictly confidential
                    until confirmed by British Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Quarton</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d291-f1" n="32" xml:id="d291-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d291-f2" n="33" xml:id="d291-f2-content">
                <p>The Consul General at St. John’s informed the Department in his telegram of
                    February 16, 2 p.m., that the “Bermuda system of landing certificates applying
                    vessels under 200 tons has been approved by Dominion Office and will be in
                    effect from 12 o’clock midnight tonight.” (811–114 Newfoundland/122)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
